# The Delta engine. Pinned to ORIGINAL UPSTREAM as of 2026-08-12: the patch set is EMPTY, so there is
# no fork branch left to carry and the url points at clast-project rather than the cmettler fork. That
# was the branch model's stated goal ("run on original upstream engineered-wood"), not a shortcut — see
# docs/ew-master-migration.md §THE 2026-08-12 PIN ONTO UPSTREAM.
#
# ⚠ TO OFFER A PATCH AGAIN you need the fork back as a push target, because this url is read-only to us:
#     git -C engineered-wood remote add fork https://github.com/cmettler/engineered-wood.git
# Carry the patch on a `fabricator-patches-v<n>` branch there, push it, and point url+branch at the fork
# for as long as the set is non-empty — a pin nobody can fetch breaks every clone, and release tags pin
# EW shas forever. Cut such a branch FRESH off upstream/main; the old v1/v2/v3 lineages are dead.
#
# ⚠ `branch = main` matters ONLY to `git submodule update --remote`, which would move the pin to the
# CURRENT upstream tip. An ordinary `git submodule update` uses the recorded sha. Bump deliberately.
[submodule "engineered-wood"]
	path = engineered-wood
	url = https://github.com/clast-project/engineered-wood.git
	branch = main
[submodule "DuckDB.ExtensionKit"]
	path = DuckDB.ExtensionKit
	url = https://github.com/Giorgi/DuckDB.ExtensionKit.git
# The DuckDB we build against. Pinned to a RELEASE TAG sha (currently v1.5.5), not a branch tip:
# this repo's branch (v1.5-variegata) tracks the 1.5 line, and the pin moves tag by tag within it.
# No `branch =` line on purpose — `git submodule update --remote` would jump to an unreleased tip.
# shallow: a depth-1 checkout has no tag context, so the build still needs -DOVERRIDE_GIT_DESCRIBE.
[submodule "duckdb"]
	path = duckdb
	url = https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb.git
	shallow = true
# Build tooling (makefiles, vcpkg ports, append_extension_metadata.py). By convention its version
# matches the DuckDB version — upstream branches are per-patch, so this is the v1.5.5 branch sha.
[submodule "extension-ci-tools"]
	path = extension-ci-tools
	url = https://github.com/duckdb/extension-ci-tools.git
	shallow = true
